                                 -(@)+(.)+(*) 

The Hittites used logograms extensively, because a single sign could be much
shorter than the half dozen or so needed to spell out a word. Sometimes,
though, they would write the Hittite ending onto the logogram for clarity: GIR₂
means “knife” in general, but GIR₂-an is specifically the nominative or
accusative form of “knife”, GIR₂-aš the genitive, GIR₂-az the ablative, and so
on.

