> nu=kan lú ninda.dù.dù kuenun
This sentence, “nu=kan lú ninda.dù.dù kuenun”, is difficult to interpret. There
should be an ablative noun.

This tablet is meant to teach you about the ablative case, so some verbs will
require it even if they didn’t before.

> * Now that we have the ablative case, we need to use it
> nu=kan lú ninda.dù.dù hattaluwaz kuenun
Nu=kan LU₂^NINDA.DU₃.DU₃ lukkandaz GIŠ^ḫattaluwaz kuenun.

Presumably through some manner of blunt force.

While the door bolt from tablet 1 reappears here, no mention is made of the
dammuri-object. It is unclear what has happened to it, or what it might have
been used for—unfortunate, since that might have given us more clues about its
nature!

